{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1 - Find your way around",
  "description": "Map a prompt to draft proposals, verified output, and benchmark results. About 10 minutes.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "pattern": "^\\#\\ DFlash\\ —\\ an\\ independent\\ starting\\ point$",
      "title": "The purpose of this code",
      "description": "Goal: identify the major components before reading their internals. A smaller draft model proposes several tokens at once. A larger target model verifies them and determines which continuation is retained. DFlash aims to reduce generation time while preserving target decoding behavior. This starts from upstream DFlash and DFlash2 and adds an optional token-only secondary drafter. The original drafting path remains the default; no training loop is included. Assume basic Python; tensor notation is introduced in tour 3."
    },
    {
      "file": "pyproject.toml",
      "pattern": "^dflash\\ =\\ \"dflash\\.cli:main\"$",
      "title": "Find the entry point",
      "description": "Installing this checkout creates the `dflash` command, routed here to `dflash.cli:main`. Without installing it, `python3 -m dflash.cli --help` works from the repository root. The `local` extra selects platform-specific inference dependencies; reading the tours needs no weights.\n\nCheckpoint 1A: Which module receives `dflash generate transformers ...` first, and which function eventually owns its decoding loop? Follow the next two steps before answering."
    },
    {
      "file": "dflash/cli.py",
      "pattern": "^def\\ main\\(argv=None\\)\\ \\->\\ None:$",
      "title": "Choose the operation and backend",
      "description": "The parser selects `generate` or `benchmark`, then a backend: `transformers`, `mlx`, or `openai`. The first two run local models and require `--draft`; the third sends requests to an existing compatible server. Generation dispatches to `_generate_transformers`, `_generate_mlx`, or `_generate_openai`. Benchmarking goes through `benchmark.run`. Input flags select a path through shared helpers; these are not three aliases for one identical implementation."
    },
    {
      "file": "dflash/benchmark.py",
      "pattern": "^def\\ load_transformers_models\\(model_id:\\ str,\\ draft_id:\\ str,\\ device\\):$",
      "title": "Load compatible models and a tokenizer",
      "description": "This loader returns `(target, draft, tokenizer)`. The tokenizer belongs to the target checkpoint, so the draft and verifier compare token IDs in that vocabulary. The draft checkpoint configuration selects DFlash or DFlash2, and both models enter evaluation mode. The CLI formats messages using the chat template before tokenizing them. Loading models can download weights; inspecting this function does not."
    },
    {
      "file": "dflash/model.py",
      "pattern": "^def\\ dflash_generate\\($",
      "title": "One loop decides which tokens survive",
      "description": "The target first selects an anchor token. DFlash then proposes the other positions of a block. The target verifies those proposals, retains a matching prefix in greedy mode, and supplies a correction or bonus.\n\nCheckpoint 1B: If `block_size=16`, how many positions are unverified draft proposals? Tour 2 follows the loop; tour 3 follows the draft model. A larger proposed block does not mean every token will be accepted."
    },
    {
      "file": "dflash/benchmark.py",
      "pattern": "^def _print_decode_summary\\($",
      "title": "Measure the result",
      "description": "Local benchmarks compare a baseline with speculative decoding and print throughput, speedup, and acceptance summaries. These are timing and generation statistics, not task-accuracy grades. In particular, the recorded acceptance lengths count newly produced tokens per round, including the correction/bonus; they are not always the number of accepted draft proposals. Tour 5 works through the exact denominators and measurement limits."
    },
    {
      "file": "dflash/__init__.py",
      "pattern": "^def\\ __getattr__\\(name\\):$",
      "title": "Explore without loading a model",
      "description": "Model imports are lazy, so CLI help can be read without the tensor libraries. Run `python3 -m dflash.cli --help` and `python3 scripts/validate_tours.py`. Then close this explanation and draw: CLI → loader/template → drafter → target verifier → retained output. Add a separate arrow for benchmark reporting. Check 1A and 1B in [the answer key](./docs/TOUR_CHECKPOINTS.md). Optional exploration: inspect `_generate_openai` and identify what computation is delegated to the server."
    }
  ],
  "isPrimary": true,
  "nextTour": "2 - Trace one greedy decoding block"
}
